  "solution": {
    "text": "For a distribution of random variable $x$, $\\alpha=P\\left(X^6 \\lt 3\\right)=P\\left(X^6=1\\right)+P\\left(X^6=2\\right)$\n$\\begin{aligned} & =\\lambda+2 \\lambda=3 \\lambda \\\\ & \\text { and } \\beta=P\\left(X^6 \\lt 2\\right)=P\\left(X^6=3\\right)+P\\left(X^6=4\\right) \\\\ & =3 \\lambda+4 \\lambda=3 \\lambda \\\\ & \\therefore \\quad \\alpha: \\beta=3: 7\\end{aligned}$",
